From c80c5e2b62ae378fe86bf10e24e22877c2672763 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:19:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: V2 legacy-index parity tooling

- chronik-native-lotus-v2-dump dumps a V2 node's legacy Chronik env with
  the six V2 group tables next to the eCash tables.
- On the V2 tier, the parity record lists the branch roots and asset IDs
  of native output frames, and the WS corpus subscribes to them as
  "v2-branch", "taproot" and "v2-asset" (strict, set, mixed and
  payload-size error sessions).
- compare.py accepts route-scoped patterns ROUTE::PATH; the V2 tier
  accepts "/validate-tx::Tx.txid", the design C1 section 1.2 defect (the
  Rust bridge reports one constant legacy-shaped txid for decoded native
  V2 txs; the native host reports the real one).

Rust (build/v2-rust) vs native, 120 blocks, --no-tokens: 17,322 HTTP
requests (17,263 identical, 59 parsed-equal, all accepted), 81 WS
sessions identical, 4 dumps equal.

Tier: V2
